WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.910
Welcome to Kashmir!

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:08.380
Do you want to escape from the
stress of the city?

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:17.890
Here you will find beautiful valleys, breath
taking nature, ancient cultures and…

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.859
Bombs!

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:22.289
Terrorist attacks, constant bombings and
systematic violence!

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:25.950
Yeah, Kashmir is the last place on
Earth where you wanna go.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:30.160
And, in the last months, this
region situated between India and Pakistan

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.390
has been on
the news headlines… again.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.240
Could it be the scenario for a
nuclear war?

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.240
Or maybe not?

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:46.829
In this video, we are gonna tell
you that story.

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:50.380
There are just 3 sport events what gather
more than a

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.700
billion people in audience worldwide: the
Opening of an

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.739
Olympic Game, the final of a Soccer World
Cup and… a

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:58.120
India-Pakistan cricket tournament.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.739
Yes, you heard this right.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:06.579
Cricket is the national sport both
in India and Pakistan: two of the most populated

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:08.469
countries
on the planet.

00:01:08.469 --> 00:01:12.779
And the rivalry between them goes way
beyond sports…

00:01:12.779 --> 00:01:18.569
Kashmir Suffers From the Worst Attack There
in 30 Years

00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:20.420
And believe me, this is not a small thing.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.119
Both India and
Pakistan have nuclear weapons.

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:26.189
The main reason of their
fights is a region called Kashmir.

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:29.369
Both countries are in
dispute for the control of this area.

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:33.840
So, in February 2019, a
terrorist group called JAISH-E-MOHAMMED organized

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.250
one
of the worst terrorist attacks in Kashmir.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.810
And India
answered with the first bombing in Pakistani

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.569
territory in
decades.

00:01:41.569 --> 00:01:44.600
The situation couldn’t be more tense.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:50.729
Are we
going to witness a nuclear war?

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:54.490
Why India and Pakistan
hate each other so much?

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.719
Today we are going to answer to
all of this questions.

00:01:55.719 --> 00:02:00.109
And we are going to do it with the help
of our friend Xander Snyder, a political analyst

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:02.880
and one the
voices from RECONSIDER MEDIA podcast that

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.349
you often
hear on our videos.

00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:08.879
Hello Simon and hello to all the VisualPolitik
subscribers!

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:12.780
As
you say, India and Pakistan are in what we

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.630
call a ‘mexican
standoff’ situation.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:24.011
Today we are going to talk a lot about
nuclear weapons and, more importantly, nuclear

00:02:24.011 --> 00:02:25.011
doctrines.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.959
Can all of this end up in a nuclear war?

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:28.500
I don’t think so but
we will see…

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.739
Well, today we are going to answer all of
this questions but,

00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:35.530
before we do, let’s take a look back at
the history.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:42.349
CLASH OF THE TITANS
After Worl War II, all the Indian territories

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:44.519
became
independent from the British Empire.

00:02:44.519 --> 00:02:46.170
But there was a
problem.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.970
There were two big religious groups here:
Muslims

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.260
on one hand and Hinduists on the other.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.810
So what did UK
do?

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.859
Easy: they sent all the Muslims to one place
and called

00:02:55.859 --> 00:02:58.469
that Pakistan, and then, they sent all the
Hindis to another

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:00.519
and called that India.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:04.340
But there was still one problem: there

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.319
were many areas where it was not clear if
there was a

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.280
Muslim or a Hindi majority.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.379
Kashmir was one of those.

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:13.640
Basically, most of the Kashmir citizens were
Muslim but

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:17.499
their governor, their MAHARAJA, happened to
be Indian.

00:03:17.499 --> 00:03:20.150
This is why they accepted that Kashmir would
be an

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.620
independent nation.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.420
Everyone was happy, right?

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.920
Well… the opposite was true.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.569
Just two months after
Kashmir declaring it’s independency, Pakistan

00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:35.569
invaded
then.

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:41.390
So the MAHARAJA asked India for help.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:45.049
This is how those brand new states: India
and Pakistan,

00:03:45.049 --> 00:03:46.049
started a war.

00:03:46.049 --> 00:03:50.030
The result, apart from a bloodbath, is that
in

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:54.019
1949, Kashmir was split between two parts:
one for India

00:03:54.019 --> 00:03:55.129
and one for Pakistan.

00:03:55.129 --> 00:03:59.469
But if you thought a border was
enough to make everybody agree… you are

00:03:59.469 --> 00:04:00.469
wrong again.

00:04:00.469 --> 00:04:03.680
These two countries had even 3 wars later
on for the control

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.510
of the whole region.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.749
Wars between India and Pakistan followed always
the same

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:11.690
pattern: Pakistan starts them and India wins
them.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:18.350
At the
end of the day, they are bigger and have more

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:19.350
money.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.329
We are already in the 60s.

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:26.190
Back then, the Indian prime
minister was this woman you see on the screen:

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.710
INDIRA
GANDHI.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.960
And there are two things you should now about
her.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.400
First, she had no familiar connection whatsoever
with

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.400
MAHATMA GANDHI.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.639
The second one is that she had
nothing to do with peace and non violence.

00:04:38.639 --> 00:04:41.599
Basically, we
are talking about a woman who forced 6 million

00:04:41.599 --> 00:04:43.160
poor people
to go for vasectomy.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.160
Just like that.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.919
So one day, this woman,
annoyed as she was by the Pakistani attacks,

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.160
said ‘FUCK
IT!

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.810
Let’s get some nukes!.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:54.270
In the year 1967 India started its nuclear
program.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.690
Since
then, Pakistani army didn’t dare to, directly

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.600
attack their now
nuclear neighbour.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:04.560
Instead, Kashmir citizens have been
suffering neverending attacks from all kind

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.729
of Pakistani
terrorist groups.

00:05:06.729 --> 00:05:10.500
And if terrorism was not enough, Indian
government doesn’t fuck around either.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.470
Since 1990,
Kashmir is under martial law.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.030
This means constant
repression to the citizens.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:20.710
And if you thought the situation
couldn’t get any more complicated… wait.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:22.590
Because in 1998
things got a twist.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:28.360
Let’s have a look at it.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:32.000
MEXICAN STANDOFF
Fighting a nuclear country is like playing

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.520
cricket without
bats.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.090
This is why, even though Pakistan is poorer
than

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:39.020
India, ZULKIFAR ALI BHUTTO, who was the president
of

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.220
Pakistan back then, had it clear.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:47.530
“We will eat grass or leaves, even go hungry,
but we will

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.800
get one of our own (nuke)” – Zulfikar
Ali Bhutto

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.229
This is how in the year 1998, Pakistan got
it’s first nuclear

00:05:55.229 --> 00:05:56.569
tests.

00:05:56.569 --> 00:05:59.330
Pakistan has been obligued to exercise the
nuclear option

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.490
due to recognization of India`s nuclear program.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:09.020
This has
led to the collapse of the existential deterrence

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:12.789
and had
radically altered the strategic balance in

00:06:12.789 --> 00:06:13.789
our region.

00:06:13.789 --> 00:06:15.699
And this is how we get to the Mexican standoff.

00:06:15.699 --> 00:06:17.979
A Mexican
standoff is a situation where two opponents

00:06:17.979 --> 00:06:19.449
are on the
same conditions.

00:06:19.449 --> 00:06:23.180
This way, both are waiting for the other to
make a false move.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.449
But even though both India and Pakistan have
now nuclear

00:06:26.449 --> 00:06:29.560
bombs, there is one thing where they differ:
their nuclear

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.730
doctrines.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.879
India has a ‘no first use’ doctrine.

00:06:32.879 --> 00:06:36.170
This means they are
ready to use their nukes only if they have

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:42.509
been attacked
with the same kind of weapons before.

00:06:42.509 --> 00:06:44.500
Pakistan is a different animal.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:48.470
They could use their atomic
weapons as soon as there are invaded.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.729
This means that,
even if India wouldn’t use nukes on an attack,

00:06:49.729 --> 00:06:50.729
they could
use them.

00:06:50.729 --> 00:06:52.300
In this doctrine, tactical weapons play a
very

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.300
important role.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.090
You see, when it comes to nuclear weapons,
there are two

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.720
different classes: strategic and tactical
ones.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.400
Strategic
weapons are those that can wipe out an entire

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:09.789
city and can
be sent to thousands of miles away.

00:07:09.789 --> 00:07:15.740
Tactical ones are
designed to be used on the battle field.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:35.659
So well, last January, Pakistan made this
test.

00:07:35.659 --> 00:07:39.659
Pakistan Equips Military With Tactical Nuke-capable
Missile

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:44.810
In other words, Pakistan compensates their
smaller military

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.770
might with a more aggresive nuclear doctrine.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.139
If India
attacks them, they could use the tactical

00:07:49.139 --> 00:07:52.690
weapons easily
and even destroy the nuclear silos on Indian

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:53.690
territory.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.379
And if
you though this is a very irresponsible nuclear

00:07:55.379 --> 00:08:00.900
doctrine for a
country, wait because you haven’t seen anything!

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:03.639
In Pakistan, the nuclear button is not on
the government’s

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:05.330
hand but on the army’s hand.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:09.039
In this country, the military
and the government go on different ways.

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:10.039
And oh boy!

00:08:10.039 --> 00:08:13.760
The
Pakistani army is pretty scary.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:17.250
Basically, there are many reasons to believe
the army is

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:20.110
supporting several terrorist organizations.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:24.379
And this explains
news like this one.

00:08:24.379 --> 00:08:28.250
For example…

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:33.810
Do you remember Osama Bin Laden?

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:36.700
Do
you remember where we was finally found?

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.810
Exactly!

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:38.960
In
Pakistan.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:44.140
More specifically, next to the KAKUL military
Academy, which is short of the Pakistany equivalent

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:45.140
to
West Point.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:48.360
And what kind of terrorist organizations might
be allegedly

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.340
connected to the military?

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.950
On one hand, we have some
jihadist groups supporting the talibans in

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.420
Afghanistan.

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:57.750
On
the other hand we have other groups like JAISH-E-

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.760
MOHAMMED that fight for the independency of
Kashmir.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.730
So no matter how hard the Islamabad government
tries to

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.560
close ties with New Delhi, both the Pakistani
army and the

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.290
terrorist make all those plans backfire.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:12.930
And what does India do to this?

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:14.880
Basically, improving their
nuclear arsenal.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.210
And what do you do when your rivalling
neighbour knows where do you have all your

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:18.210
nuclear silos?

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.700
Well… we are going to tell you right now.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.280
NUCLEAR WAR?

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:26.910
Would you imagine somebody like JOHN ELWAY,
the

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:29.760
legendary sportsman, becoming the American
president?

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.100
Well, this is what happened in Pakistan.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.950
Their new
president is IMRAR KHAN, the man who made

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.170
his country
win the cricket world cup.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:40.790
Just like his predecessors, IMRAN KHAN traed
to improve

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.690
the relationships with India.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:46.151
And this is when the terrorist
from JAISH-E-MOHAMMED organized the worse

00:09:46.151 --> 00:09:49.120
massacre
in Kashmir in the latest decades.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.500
And this is when Narendra Modi said something
like:

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.310
Pakistan, come over here.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:58.030
Look,
we have a lottery and the winner gets a punch

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.130
in the face...

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.130
And guess what!

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:03.270
You have all the tickets!!!!

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:08.530
In other words, for the first time in decades,
Indian army

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.500
bombed Pakistani territory.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.390
This means they didn’t attack
the Pakistani part of Kashmir but Pakistan

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:15.390
itself.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.090
But hold on
just a second because this is not the end

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.090
of the story!

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.710
Do
you remember that Mexican standoff situation?

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:21.710
So well…

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:24.020
India has made a hell of a move.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:29.950
And this move has a
name: INS ARIHANT, the so called ‘enemies

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:31.840
destructor’.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:36.370
Nuclear submarine INS Arihant completes patrol,
country’s

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:40.710
N-triad operational
Do you remember when I told you that Pakistan

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:43.200
could use
their strategic weapons to destroy Indian

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.200
nuclear silos?

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:45.200
So

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.200
well…

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.200
Indians are aware of this and this is why
they got

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.200
nuclear submarines.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:51.590
The advantage of a nuclear submarine
is that you can have your arsenal moving all

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:53.190
the time under
the water.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.390
It is harder to find and, therefore, harder
to

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.390
destroy.

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:59.310
And this is why Pakistani army was so nervous.

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:01.800
And this is the point where media started
talking about a

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.370
would-be nuclear war.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.070
But… is this really possible?

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.750
Well…
we at VisualPolitik don’t really think so.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.750
Why?

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:11.200
Well… first of all, even though India attacked
Pakistan, they

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:13.440
just bombed some terrorist training camps.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:16.350
This means they
didn’t actually crossed the red lines for

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.130
what Pakistan
considers an invasion.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:20.170
So what was Islamabad’s answer to this?

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.170
Well… some air
strikes.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.820
But let’s be honest, they are the last ones
wanting a

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:24.820
nuclear war.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.910
If not, look at what the former Pakistani
President said.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:36.080
If We Attack With 1 Nuke, India May Finish
Us With 20&amp;quot;:

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:39.260
Pervez Musharraf
This explains why Pakistan didn’t wait any

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.350
longer than 3
days to release the Indian pilot they captured.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.100
And… in
case they would be tempted, at some point,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.230
to stroke
back…

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:48.740
India has made things very, very clear.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:55.360
Indian Navy deploys aircraft carrier &amp;amp;
nuclear subs to deter

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.980
‘misadventures’ by Pakistan

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.330
So, again, so far it seems that no country
is really thinking

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.260
about an actual nuclear war.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.820
So then… who is winning with
all of this?

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.860
Well… so far, the most clear winner is Narendra
Modi, the

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:08.860
Indian Prime Minister.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:12.060
Yes, my dear viewers, India is
celebrating a presidential election.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:23.690
And all this conflict with
Pakistan has helped Modi to raise in the polls.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:27.160
But don’t worry because in the following
weeks, we will talk

